<title>USA: RomTech says shrs fall from WS shutdown.</title>
<headline>RomTech says shrs fall from WS shutdown.</headline>
<dateline>LANGHORNE, Pa. 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>RomTech Inc said on Friday that the company's stock price has been hurt from the shutdown and subsequent liquidation of WS Clearing, of Glendale, Calif.</p>
<p>BG Capital, a market maker for the company's stock, used WS Clearing to clear its trades, a spokesman for RomTech said.</p>
<p>RomTech shares traded at 3-5/8, off 5/8, on 31,400 shares of volume.</p>
